====== TP-Link TL-MR10U ======

{{section>meta:infobox:432_warning#infobox_for_dataentries&noheader&nofooter&noeditbutton}}

{{ media:tplink:tl-mr10u:tl-mr10u.jpg?200|}}

A portable router with an onboard 2600mAh battery. Hardware similar to [[toh:tp-link:TL-MR3040]] and [[toh:tp-link:TL-WR703N]]. See also [[toh:tp-link:tl-mr11u|TL-MR11U]], [[toh:tp-link:tl-mr12u|TL-MR12U]] and [[toh:tp-link:tl-mr13u|TL-MR13U]].

**Note:** Many of these routers are marketed as a //"3G travel router"// but  **none actually include a 3G modem** - Rather, it's a marketing term that refers to the fact that the OEM firmware supports USB 3G modems because it contains drivers for USB modems.


